conflict.description:
**{automation_a}** sets `{entity}` to **{value_a}** while **{automation_b}** sets it to **{value_b}** at the same moment.

Shared trigger: {trigger}
Situation: {situation}

Which one wins depends on timing. Add a condition so only one of them acts in this situation, or merge the logic into one automation.

loop.description:
These automations can keep triggering each other:

{lines}

Check whether a condition breaks the chain – for example, only act when the target state is not reached yet.

self_trigger.description:
**{automation}** changes an entity it listens to itself and can therefore trigger again:

{lines}

A condition such as "only if the state is not already correct" or a `to:` in the trigger prevents the repetition.
